# SRS & Practice

## SRS model

- **Not** SM-2/Anki — multi-track Leitner per `(word, channel)`
- 4 channels: meaning, listening, pinyin, sentence
- Intervals in `src/config/constants.ts`: `CN_SRS_INTERVALS_MINUTES` (10m → 360d)
- Ramp: listening/pinyin due only after `meaningIntervalIdx >= CN_RAMP_MEANING_INTERVAL_IDX` (`channelRamp.ts`)
- First wrong on channel: 30m cooldown (`CN_FIRST_WRONG_RETRY_MINUTES`)
- Lapse floor: index 1 (1 day), not reset to 10 minutes
- Due eligibility: schedule + ramp + cooldown — **no** lifetime-rate weak bypass in `isChannelDue`
- Priority: channel-only (overdue, weakness with sample weight) — no `p.state` boost
- Sentence unlock when meaning reaches familiar (idx ≥ 2)

## Due query perf

- SQL superset prefilter: `buildDueCandidateWhere` in `cnSrsDueQuery.ts`
- JS `isChannelDue` remains source of truth
- Indexes on `userId + *DueAt` per channel

## Practice

- **6 core question types** — `coreQuestionTypes.ts`, taxonomy in `practiceTaxonomy.ts`
- Question generation: `generateQuestions.ts`
- Modes filter allowed types; fallback to core/listening if channel locked

## Known perf caveats

- `listUserSets` calls `countDueAndWeak` per set (N+1 risk)

